age: Unlocking dependable responses with Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform’s Agentic RAG  UNLOCKING DEPENDABLE RESPONSES WITH GEMINI ENTERPRISE AGENT PLATFORM’S AGENTIC RAG  June 5, 2026  Cyrus Rash...",{"_267":268,"_269":270,"_271":268},1780617600,{"_349":397,"_351":-5,"_352":398,"_354":399,"_62":400,"_356":401,"_47":402,"_359":-5,"_50":376,"_377":403,"_379":404,"_154":381,"_382":-5,"_383":-5},{"_349":370,"_351":-5,"_352":371,"_354":372,"_62":373,"_356":374,"_47":375,"_359":-5,"_50":376,"_377":378,"_379":380,"_154":381,"_382":-5,"_383":-5},{"_349":350,"_351":-5,"_352":353,"_354":353,"_62":355,"_356":357,"_47":358,"_359":-5,"_50":360,"_361":362,"_363":14},"matched_text"," ","prefix","start_idx",1757,"end_idx",[],"refs",[],"","prompt_text","sources_footnote","sources",[364,365],"has_images",{"_53":368,"_41":236,"_266":369},{"_53":366,"_41":242,"_266":367},"The AI context gap: Enterprise AI organizations have a trust problem, not a retrieval problem — and most are still building the fix | VentureBeat","Venturebeat","Retrieval-augmented generation for natural language processing: a survey | Artificial Intelligence Review | Springer Nature Link","Springer","citeturn0search3turn0search10",1134,1167,[239,240,241,242],[],"([Venturebeat](https://venturebeat.com/ai/the-ai-context-gap-enterprise-ai-organizations-have-a-trust-problem-not-a-retrieval-problem-and-most-are-still-building-the-fix?utm_source=chatgpt.com))","grouped_webpages","items",[384],"fallback_items",[],"done","error","style",{"_53":366,"_41":242,"_266":367,"_264":385,"_260":358,"_386":-5,"_387":388,"_356":389,"_390":-5,"_391":-5},1784764800,"attribution_segments","supporting_websites",[395],[392,393],"hue","attributions",{"_267":268,"_269":270,"_271":394},{"_267":268,"_269":270,"_271":272},3,{"_53":259,"_41":240,"_264":-5,"_260":358,"_266":396},"Unstructured","citeturn0search8turn0search0",227,259,[235,236,237,238],[],"([Springer](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10462-026-11605-7?utm_source=chatgpt.com))",[405],[],{"_53":368,"_41":236,"_266":369,"_264":406,"_260":358,"_386":-5,"_387":407,"_356":408,"_390":-5,"_391":-5},1780272000,[412],[409,410],{"_267":268,"_269":270,"_271":411},{"_267":268,"_269":270,"_271":268},8,{"_53":342,"_41":238,"_264":-5,"_260":358,"_266":413},"Google Research",[193],[416],"In the **2026 market context**, I would currently rate your project around **7.5/10**. RAG itself is already a mature and widely used architecture for AI agents, so simply building another RAG chatbot would not be very unique. citeturn0search8turn0search0\n\nWhat makes your project more interesting is the **specific problem you are solving: conversation/agent knowledge transfer**. Instead of asking a user to manually explain everything to a new AI agent, your system takes an existing public conversation, extracts the knowledge, retrieves the relevant information, and converts it into a structured knowledge document that another agent can use. That gives your project a clear product-level use case rather than being just a RAG demonstration.\n\nI would break the rating down like this: **Idea: 8.5/10, Technical implementation: 7/10 currently, Market relevance: 8/10, Uniqueness: 7.5/10, Potential: 9/10.** The biggest opportunity is to make the final system more than “retrieve → LLM → PDF.” Current enterprise RAG is moving toward better retrieval, reranking, validation, agentic retrieval, and reliable context management. citeturn0search3turn0search10\n\nIf you add things like **automatic extraction of user preferences, important decisions, behavioral patterns, conversation summaries, confidence/source tracking, contradiction detection, structured memory, and an export format that can actually be consumed by another AI agent**, I would consider it closer to **9/10 as a portfolio/startup project**. The strongest positioning would be: **“A conversation-to-agent-memory system that transfers the knowledge and context of an existing AI interaction to a new agent.”** That sounds considerably stronger than simply calling it a RAG project.",{"_418":419},"real_author","tool:web",{"_141":220,"_148":423,"_54":424,"_152":425,"_154":155,"_156":14,"_157":158,"_159":426,"_161":162},"f83d7455-78ad-46cd-b8de-60f5611d2f6c",[203],{"_199":200,"_159":438},1788541184.864672,{"_194":436,"_152":437},{"_427":428,"_429":158,"_430":431,"_432":433,"_434":435,"_177":178,"_179":233,"_181":182,"_183":234,"_185":234,"_174":109,"_186":109,"_66":67,"_187":14,"_188":421,"_189":10},"reasoning_status","reasoning_ended","finished_duration_sec","reasoning_start_time",1788541183.3082216,"reasoning_end_time",1788541184.833101,"reasoning_recap_type","hide_all","reasoning_recap","Worked for a couple of seconds",{},{"_141":421,"_148":442,"_54":443,"_152":444,"_154":155,"_156":14,"_157":158,"_159":445,"_161":162},"f6a2d866-b175-45e5-8f1d-77a04d2b807e",[220],{"_199":200,"_159":481},1788541184.853553,{"_194":471,"_471":472,"_473":474},{"_446":447,"_427":448,"_449":450,"_451":452,"_430":431,"_177":178,"_179":233,"_181":182,"_183":234,"_185":234,"_174":109,"_186":109,"_66":67,"_187":14,"_188":453,"_189":10},"inline_cot_expandable_content",{"_467":468},"is_reasoning","tool_summary_type","web","tool_icons",[454,455,456,457,458,459,460,461,462,463,464,465,466],"21c5de19-3ab3-4fd4-93b8-3408ebdbbc4a","https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=research.google&sz=128","https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.eicta.iitk.ac.in&sz=128","https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=ragweaver.ai&sz=128","https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=venturebeat.com&sz=128","https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=aclanthology.org&sz=128","https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=blog.agentsarchitects.ai&sz=128","https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.exploreagentic.ai&sz=128","https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=ragbible.com&sz=128","https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.reddit.com&sz=128","https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=link.springer.com&sz=